  "summary": "This scope covers 41 validated functions spanning four runtime concerns. The largest family is 32 thiscall constructors of DirectX texture/surface/render-buffer objects, all invoked from DirectXTextureSurfaceFactoryDispatchingFourCCCod (0x0050B8A9) and each performing a shared base initialization through one of three helpers (DirectXTextureCreationWithMipmapChain 0x00507496, DirectXTextureSurfaceFormatInitialization 0x0050AFE2, or RenderBufferVertexAllocator 0x0050A7E1) followed by installation of a distinct vtable pointer at this+0x0. The distinct vtable per constructor implies a distinct (unnamed) class each, but only the shared construction pattern is evidenced. Two free CPU feature detectors (0x0050FD4E SSE/SSE2, 0x005171D0 MMX/3DNow-class/AMD) wrap CPUID in SEH; they use incompatible flag-bit schemes and are grouped only by shared concern. One size-parameterized zero-allocator (0x00517E43) dispatches request codes 1 and 2 to 412- and 64-byte blocks. The MPEG audio decoder open path (0x0052E090, name derived from the aCmpegbaseOpenG string, GUESS owner 'CMpegBase') performs deferred deactivation, sync-word storage, audio-device assertion and buffer timing/sizing. Four functions (0x00534D50, 0x00534E70, 0x00535560, 0x00535620) implement a buffered-stream block reader with byte reader, block-header parser, dword packer and per-frame context reset. A vtable-destructor thunk (0x0052D8C0) forwards to an un-evidenced VirtualCleanup. All grouping into classes is DERIVED/GUESS: no RTTI, vtable-member or runtime ownership evidence exists in this packet.",
